# Pinned from the real red run of 2026-07-28 with the injection applied.
#
# The injection removes both halves of the fix — boundary validation (defect 1)
# and the writer's compose->re-parse guard (defect 2) — which is exactly the
# state the ledger was bricked from on 2026-07-26.
exit: 101

# The write is ACCEPTED. That acceptance is the defect: the operator gets a
# tx_id back and has no signal until the next read.
contains: test multi_line_reason_is_refused_and_project_ledger_still_parses ... FAILED
contains: test multi_line_reason_is_refused_and_home_ledger_still_parses ... FAILED
contains: a multi-line reason must be refused, never appended

# The production symptom itself, logged by the daemon's own index refresh
# immediately after the accepted append: the append-only ledger no longer
# parses, so every subsequent verb fails. Reproduced on BOTH destinations —
# the project ledger and the $ORGASMIC_HOME/state/tx home file.
contains: malformed property drawer entry: blank line inside property drawer

# `--extra KEY=VALUE` is the same hole: the injected prose pushes the later
# properties out of the drawer, so a plain prose line is read as a property.
contains: test multi_line_extra_value_is_refused_and_nothing_is_written ... FAILED

# The supported single-line shapes must keep passing even on the injected
# tree: this defect is about what the writer ACCEPTS, not about breaking
# ordinary writes. A red run where this also fails means the injection
# widened past the defect.
contains: test ledger_still_parses_after_every_supported_write ... ok
